-- | OpenZeppelin Pausable — a standalone, token-agnostic emergency-stop switch.
--
-- This is the Daml analogue of OpenZeppelin's `Pausable.sol`: a single boolean
-- the authority can flip, plus a guard (`whenNotPaused`) that gated operations
-- call to refuse work while paused. It is deliberately independent — it carries
-- no role type and depends on no other OpenZeppelin package, so a project that
-- wants only a pause switch imports only this DAR.
--
-- # Keyless model (Daml-LF 2.1)
-- LF 2.1 has no contract keys, so there is no global "is the registry paused?"
-- lookup. Instead the live `PauseState` is a contract that gated operations
-- read by `ContractId` (disclosed to them by the pauser) and check via
-- `whenNotPaused`. "Pause" is therefore *origination control*: new operations
-- that consult the flag refuse to start while paused; already-committed work is
-- unaffected — the only robustly enforceable pause semantic on a UTXO ledger.
--
-- # Semantics vs. Solidity
-- Solidity stores `_paused` in contract storage and reads it via a modifier.
-- Here the flag lives in an immutable `PauseState` contract; flipping it
-- archives the old contract and creates the next one (state transition by
-- re-creation, as everywhere in Daml).
module OpenZeppelin.Pausable where

-- | The current pause state of a resource, administered by `pauser`.
--
-- Signatories: `pauser` (the only authority over the switch).
-- Observers: none on the template itself — consumers are granted read access by
--   explicit disclosure of this contract's `ContractId` (the pauser discloses
--   the active `PauseState` to the operations that gate on it). Keeping the
--   observer set empty avoids an unbounded observer-list field and keeps the
--   privacy surface minimal.
-- Controllers: `pauser` controls both choices.
-- Choices: `PauseState_Set` (flip the flag), `PauseState_Get` (read the flag).
-- Disclosed parties: whoever the pauser explicitly discloses the contract to in
--   order to let them enforce `whenNotPaused`.
-- Privacy expectations: only the pauser and explicitly-disclosed readers learn
--   the pause state.
-- Authorization assumptions: only `pauser` can create or flip the switch; the
--   contract is `pauser`-signed and therefore unforgeable.
-- Archival behavior: `PauseState_Set` is consuming — it archives the current
--   state and creates the successor; no standalone archive choice is exposed.
-- Failure modes: `PauseState_Set` rejects a redundant change (setting the flag
--   to its current value) so the on-ledger history records only real
--   transitions.
-- Upgrade and migration assumptions: 0.x, unstable; field/contract shape may
--   change before a 1.0 ADR. Not yet public API.
template PauseState
  with
    pauser : Party
      -- ^ The authority that may pause and unpause.
    paused : Bool
      -- ^ Whether the resource is currently paused.
  where
    signatory pauser

    -- | Flip the pause flag. Returns the successor contract id.
    -- Rejects a no-op change so history records only real transitions.
    choice PauseState_Set : ContractId PauseState
      with
        newPaused : Bool
      controller pauser
      do
        assertMsg ePauseRedundant (newPaused /= paused)
        create this with paused = newPaused

    -- | Read the current flag without archiving the contract.
    nonconsuming choice PauseState_Get : Bool
      controller pauser
      do
        pure paused

-- | The guard a gated operation calls, given the (fetched) pause state.
-- Fails the transaction when paused. This is the `whenNotPaused` modifier
-- analogue: a consumer fetches the disclosed `PauseState` and calls this before
-- doing origination work.
whenNotPaused : PauseState -> Update ()
whenNotPaused ps =
  assertMsg ePaused (not ps.paused)

-- | Pure predicate form, for callers that already hold the flag.
isPaused : PauseState -> Bool
isPaused ps = ps.paused

-- Error messages (inlined to keep this package dependency-free).

ePaused : Text
ePaused = "Pausable: paused"

ePauseRedundant : Text
ePauseRedundant = "Pausable: redundant pause change"
